@host = http://localhost:5100
@customerId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

### Check out the basket filled in Basket.http - expect 201 Created + Location
### The body carries only the customer id: prices come from the catalog, never from the client
POST {{host}}/api/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "{{customerId}}" }

### Check out an EMPTY basket (a fresh customer) - the domain says no; expect 422
POST {{host}}/api/checkout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222" }

### One order - expect 200 OK
GET {{host}}/api/orders/01a023b5-324f-7a47-8dc9-b91949332e3f

### All orders - expect 200 OK
GET {{host}}/api/orders

### Cancel the order - expect 204 No Content
POST {{host}}/api/orders/01a023b5-324f-7a47-8dc9-b91949332e3f/cancel

### Cancel it AGAIN - only a placed order can be cancelled; expect 422
POST {{host}}/api/orders/01a023b5-324f-7a47-8dc9-b91949332e3f/cancel
